{
  "note": [
    "What tmux puts in each format field, for the fields whose shape is not a",
    "string. Derived from format.c: FORMAT_TABLE_TIME gives time, a callback",
    "returning only \"1\" or \"0\" gives boolean, and one using an integer printf",
    "conversion gives number. Six that derivation got wrong are corrected by",
    "hand and named in the parity of this file's own test: an identity carries",
    "its sigil (%0, $0, @0) and is declared by its identity kind here; a stack",
    "or alert set is a comma-separated list and remains plain text.",
    "Eleven more come from outside format.c \u2014 cmd-list-*.c and window-copy.c \u2014",
    "where the derivation cannot see them, and are taken from the printf",
    "conversion beside them.",
    "pane_at_top and pane_at_bottom print a 0/1 int with \"%d\", so the integer",
    "rule reads them as counts; their siblings at_left and at_right return \"1\"",
    "or \"0\" directly. pane_in_mode really is a count of active modes.",
    "A field absent here is a string. tests/integration/format_types.test.ts",
    "reads this file and asserts every entry against a live server, so a claim",
    "here that tmux disagrees with fails on all four versions CI runs.",
    "history_all_bytes, session_alert, cursor_shape, cursor_colour and pane_key_mode are strings and so are absent: history_all_bytes prints six comma-separated integers with \"%u,%zu,%u,%zu,%u,%zu\", which the integer rule above would otherwise read as a number."
  ],
